  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Oxycodone IR Criteria Version 2. Original 06/23/2007; Approval 11/15/2019; Effective 1/6/2020.",
    "Formulations: tablets 5/7.5/10/15/20/30 mg; capsules 5 mg; oral solution 5 mg/5 mL; concentrated solution 20 mg/mL. The source solution criteria call the same 1 mg/mL concentration 10 mg/10 mL.",
    "Criterion 1: every request hard-rejects at the pharmacy unless a PA is on file or patient age <14 fills oxycodone solution 10 mg/10 mL post-procedure, quantity \u226490 mL. Existing PA claim adjudication remains notes only; the pediatric exception is encoded as an alternate path.",
    "Hospice, cancer or LTC pharmacy override and the pediatric exception bypass standard outpatient criteria and additional solution requirements. The closed pain indication applies on all paths.",
    "Standard outpatient: failed/intolerant to \u22652 non-opioid therapies and combination opioid inappropriate; single-agent oxycodone \u226490 mg/day OR active OxyContin ER PA with IR for breakthrough pain and all oxycodone forms \u2264160 mg/day. Criterion 9 follows the regimen OR with AND: PRN breakthrough dosing, no addictive behaviors or substance-use treatment, and state/national guidelines are shared by both standard arms.",
    "Standard solution approval additionally requires inability to use solid dosage forms. Concentrated 20 mg/mL additionally requires a documented medical condition necessitating a solution more concentrated than 10 mg/10 mL.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor addiction, abuse and misuse; serious, life-threatening or fatal respiratory depression may occur. Benzodiazepines or other CNS depressants, including alcohol, may cause profound sedation, respiratory depression, coma and death.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months with clinically meaningful chart notes showing positive response to therapy.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): Maximum Units Med List http://dhss.alaska.gov/dhcs/Pages/pharmacy/medpriorauthoriz.aspx . Duration, reauthorization and general quantity enforcement remain manual review."
  ],
